WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.490 --> 00:00:07.516
In the previous videos, you could see how we did during the winter break, 
and what's coming for this third season at Project Kamp. 

00:00:07.516 --> 00:00:10.102
Now, we're really starting to think!

00:00:10.102 --> 00:00:14.733
In this episode, we are going to renovate,
and customize a strong old car we bought.

00:00:14.733 --> 00:00:17.122
Welcome to a new Project Kamp update!

00:00:21.671 --> 00:00:24.078
We need a car for our daily work, here at the Kamp.

00:00:24.078 --> 00:00:26.864
So, we bought a second hand pickup from the 90s...

00:00:26.864 --> 00:00:28.699
Big, strong, and durable.

00:00:28.699 --> 00:00:32.534
The engine is in good condition, 
but the car needs some fixes, and maintenance...

00:00:32.534 --> 00:00:37.621
It took a while to find it, because this kind of car 
is very popular, in the Portuguese countryside...

00:00:37.621 --> 00:00:42.715
We want to give some love to this old beast,
and also, we want to have a nice customized look.

00:00:42.715 --> 00:00:46.374
So, we will have a dashboard made out of recycled wood and fabric.

00:00:47.079 --> 00:00:48.075
So, hello!

00:00:48.075 --> 00:00:50.604
Here we have our new old car!

00:00:50.604 --> 00:00:56.759
We used to have another old car too,
 but we didn't stop to repair the whole time...

00:00:56.759 --> 00:01:02.729
So, we want an old car that we are able
to repair ourselves, that is reliable...

00:01:02.729 --> 00:01:04.751
This is a big upgrade for us!

00:01:04.751 --> 00:01:09.002
We have a pickup now, where we can put a lot of materials inside...

00:01:09.002 --> 00:01:11.178
We can carry big pieces...

00:01:11.178 --> 00:01:12.736
We can carry our waste...

00:01:12.736 --> 00:01:14.962
We can carry way more people too!

00:01:14.962 --> 00:01:19.080
But, as you can see, the car is not in the best condition...

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:21.447
There's some rust problems...

00:01:21.447 --> 00:01:25.740
The box is rusting here, and creates puddles inside...

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:29.500
The wood is not that bad, but just looks a bit old.

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:33.693
Some parts of this box, as you can see, 
are not in the best condition...

00:01:34.331 --> 00:01:36.317
There's a broken part here too...

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:40.200
Little things...

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:43.230
Well, not the perfect state...

00:01:43.230 --> 00:01:46.026
A sketchy repair from the old owner.

00:01:46.026 --> 00:01:48.570
All this putty on top of the rust...

00:01:48.570 --> 00:01:50.065
Disgusting...

00:01:50.065 --> 00:01:53.232
We also need to improve the safety of it, a bit...

00:01:53.232 --> 00:01:55.509
As you can see...

00:02:07.489 --> 00:02:09.440
Almost ready...

00:02:18.681 --> 00:02:22.511
And, under the hood, we also want to make some little things.

00:02:23.786 --> 00:02:32.407
We actually got this car, because it looks bad on the outside, 
but its 'heart' is in very good condition.

00:02:32.407 --> 00:02:36.016
Still, we want to do the basic maintenance of it...

00:02:36.016 --> 00:02:38.480
Basic things, to make it last longer.

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:43.115
We will try to reuse as much parts as we can, from this car.

00:02:43.115 --> 00:02:44.427
Repair as much as we can...

00:02:44.427 --> 00:02:49.851
We will go to the scrapyard to find the same car,
 and try to get all pieces for it.

00:02:50.388 --> 00:02:52.725
Maybe, we'd find some bigger things...

00:02:52.725 --> 00:02:53.882
We hope not.

00:02:53.882 --> 00:02:57.580
We also have Hans here to help us with this!

00:02:57.849 --> 00:02:58.840
- Hello!

00:02:59.176 --> 00:03:00.199
So, this is Hans!

00:03:00.199 --> 00:03:02.473
He is a Dutch guy, who lives close by.

00:03:02.840 --> 00:03:06.869
Although, he is not part of the team, 
he is a very good friend of the project!

00:03:06.869 --> 00:03:10.746
He has such a passion for old cars, 
that he gets really fast into work!

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:15.988
So, the first thing to do:
 we will start with the basic maintenance of the car.

00:03:16.659 --> 00:03:20.455
Change filters, change oils, etcetera...

00:03:20.455 --> 00:03:22.963
To have it ready to start.

00:03:43.305 --> 00:03:45.176
- We changed the oil filter!

00:03:46.015 --> 00:03:47.155
Look at this!

00:04:00.729 --> 00:04:05.563
We think that there was a super strong mechanic, 
before working in this car...

00:04:08.617 --> 00:04:13.221
Because, it's so strongly connected, we can't get it from its connector...

00:04:13.221 --> 00:04:17.620
So, we need to put a hole inside, and turn it with the bar.

00:04:27.887 --> 00:04:28.854
- Easy job!

00:04:28.854 --> 00:04:29.881
Now, a new filter...

00:04:35.005 --> 00:04:36.863
New oil, and I'm ready!

00:04:44.025 --> 00:04:48.670
The filters and oil is ready, so let's see if the car starts again

00:05:00.520 --> 00:05:05.561
I always had my own Land Rovers in a building, 
 and I bought cheap ones.

00:05:05.561 --> 00:05:08.526
I took them apart and restored them all...

00:05:08.526 --> 00:05:09.200
- Ah, cool!

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:10.436
Do you have a Land Rover now?

00:05:10.436 --> 00:05:10.936
- No...

00:05:10.936 --> 00:05:11.545
No?

00:05:11.746 --> 00:05:13.115
I left them in Holland.

00:05:13.149 --> 00:05:17.138
Yeah, the first year I thought it was pity, 
because there's lots of roads here.

00:05:17.138 --> 00:05:19.768
It's good for a Land Rover, but now, I'm glad it's over.

00:05:19.768 --> 00:05:20.440
- Yeah?

00:05:20.469 --> 00:05:21.112
Yeah...

00:05:21.112 --> 00:05:25.645
Always in your back, always your hands broken...

00:05:25.645 --> 00:05:31.870
And now, it's good as a hobby,
but you should sometimes leave your hobbies alone...

00:05:32.440 --> 00:05:35.672
We are gonna take apart the box of the pickup now.

00:05:35.873 --> 00:05:37.407
To see what is the state...

00:05:37.407 --> 00:05:39.927
And, we will fix all that we can.

00:05:39.927 --> 00:05:42.149
There's the angle of the box.

00:05:42.149 --> 00:05:48.211
It's slightly up, which means that these two lines are not parallel...

00:05:49.386 --> 00:05:51.740
It makes that, when the bumpy roads come...

00:05:51.740 --> 00:05:53.612
Touches the car too...

00:05:53.914 --> 00:05:58.440
Another problem that it generates, 
is like it creates puddles in the box.

00:05:58.440 --> 00:05:59.982
When it rains, because it's like this.

00:05:59.982 --> 00:06:08.447
So, we will try to make it straight, to make the water go out, 
and prevent these areas from touching

00:06:08.883 --> 00:06:10.000
To be more safe.

00:06:17.316 --> 00:06:18.465
Take care of your hands, yeah?

00:06:21.854 --> 00:06:23.880
Wow, 'mooi'!*
* meaning 'nice' in Dutch

00:06:24.640 --> 00:06:25.704
It's nice like this!

00:06:29.406 --> 00:06:32.480
And the lights are not working, in your reverse light!

00:06:32.480 --> 00:06:33.548
Blinkers?

00:06:33.548 --> 00:06:34.293
This one is good!

00:06:34.293 --> 00:06:35.529
Yeah, they work!

00:06:37.497 --> 00:06:40.694
The light, its the glass that is not good...

00:07:04.881 --> 00:07:06.725
They made this on this wood...

00:07:07.262 --> 00:07:09.100
And, so, we cannot take them out...

00:07:10.912 --> 00:07:13.254
You can see that they're all rusted...

00:07:13.254 --> 00:07:17.549
I don't think it will turn, so, 
what we have to do is make new holes there...

00:07:17.549 --> 00:07:19.774
And, make the whole thing new.

00:07:43.681 --> 00:07:45.681
I've never repaired a car with a saw!

00:07:54.596 --> 00:07:56.480
Looks like new...

00:07:59.052 --> 00:08:02.000
Cut it here, Cut it here, and try to cut it here.

00:08:20.470 --> 00:08:25.346
So, we're gonna weld a big disk, in order to make it sturdy.

00:09:18.288 --> 00:09:20.000
Here we have the back bumper.

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:23.215
And, it just cracked here, so there is a hole...

00:09:23.215 --> 00:09:25.771
So, we're going to weld it together, so it's strong again.

00:09:57.393 --> 00:10:01.258
Okay, so far, we fixed the structure of the car, 
and the bottom of the box.

00:10:01.896 --> 00:10:06.244
But, we see that the beams underneath are rotten, 
and we need to remake them...

00:10:06.244 --> 00:10:09.169
So, Jaime will use one of them as a template.

00:10:09.538 --> 00:10:13.636
And, with leftover wood, that we keep in the bottom 
of the office, we will make new ones.

00:10:13.904 --> 00:10:17.922
We will protect them with the used car oil, 
that we took from the motor.

00:12:23.159 --> 00:12:28.006
After looking at it on the internet, 
I found a guy that might have some spare parts for our car.

00:12:28.610 --> 00:12:31.883
So, we're gonna meet him now, 
and see what he has there...

00:12:38.920 --> 00:12:41.200
 

00:12:41.200 --> 00:12:43.960
 

00:12:59.640 --> 00:13:01.440
 

00:13:01.440 --> 00:13:02.212
 

00:13:02.212 --> 00:13:02.712
 

00:13:03.561 --> 00:13:04.280
 

00:13:04.280 --> 00:13:06.080
 

00:13:06.580 --> 00:13:08.720
 

00:13:08.720 --> 00:13:09.600
 

00:13:09.600 --> 00:13:12.880
 

00:13:12.880 --> 00:13:14.947
 

00:13:14.947 --> 00:13:17.200
 

00:13:17.200 --> 00:13:18.400
 

00:13:18.400 --> 00:13:19.840
 

00:13:20.000 --> 00:13:22.482
So, we already have the pieces in the Kamp!

00:13:23.120 --> 00:13:27.602
Ready to be installed, and replace the pieces,
 that are broken from our car...

00:14:36.506 --> 00:14:38.506
Someone took care of his car so much!

00:14:59.320 --> 00:15:02.788
Again, we are reusing the oil we replaced from the pickup

00:15:02.788 --> 00:15:04.408
Hans says it's not really necessary...

00:15:04.408 --> 00:15:05.553
- I don't need to do this...

00:15:05.553 --> 00:15:07.873
I only do this, because it looks nice.

00:15:07.873 --> 00:15:12.636
But, we feel it will protect our leaf springs better, in the long run.

00:15:13.673 --> 00:15:16.981
We will continue now, fixing many small details, around the car...

00:15:16.981 --> 00:15:20.507
With some ingenuity, and the part we got from the scrapyard.

00:16:03.689 --> 00:16:05.840
- Yeah, like new!

00:17:06.600 --> 00:17:10.040
Time to change this annoying mirror...

00:17:30.836 --> 00:17:33.205
Yeah...
Good now!

00:17:41.664 --> 00:17:43.520
Goodmorning Hans!

00:17:53.161 --> 00:17:54.346
Very good.

00:17:54.346 --> 00:17:55.575
- Expensive, or no?

00:17:55.575 --> 00:17:56.480
Five euros.

00:17:56.480 --> 00:17:58.122
It changes the look...

00:17:58.122 --> 00:18:00.680
It does, it really does change the look, yeah...

00:18:01.936 --> 00:18:03.192
This is not safe.

00:18:10.000 --> 00:18:14.437
So, here we lost all the information about the fuses...

00:18:14.437 --> 00:18:17.150
But, we luckily found a new piece!

00:18:17.150 --> 00:18:19.308
With the right information on it...

00:18:19.308 --> 00:18:24.920
So, we can replace the fuses and replace the lid. 

00:18:45.016 --> 00:18:46.000
Done!

00:19:11.400 --> 00:19:15.560
So, we have replaced the old frame for new fresh beams!

00:19:15.560 --> 00:19:19.353
We have treated the wood with the oil, that was in the car.

00:19:19.353 --> 00:19:22.154
Now, we already put the box in place.

00:19:22.154 --> 00:19:29.026
We will treat the wood and the metal,
 to give a long life to this old box...

00:21:28.520 --> 00:21:32.140
Now, we're trying to go and see, 
if we can find some tools inside!

00:21:32.140 --> 00:21:36.550
Because, we need to do things here on the car,
with the tools of the car...

00:21:36.852 --> 00:21:42.124
But, that's a very big problem, 
because the tools are behind the seat...

00:21:42.124 --> 00:21:45.560
And the seat can't open without a rope...

00:21:45.560 --> 00:21:50.617
And, the rope has disappeared, so, 
that will be a very interesting problem...

00:21:51.322 --> 00:21:52.465
- Exactly...

00:21:56.160 --> 00:21:57.416
Look at this!

00:22:00.973 --> 00:22:02.120
- Jesus!

00:22:02.264 --> 00:22:03.280
Glass!

00:22:04.039 --> 00:22:05.244
And, nails...

00:22:13.363 --> 00:22:15.363
See if you can find-
yeah I found the rope

00:22:20.000 --> 00:22:21.280
It's antique!

00:22:22.679 --> 00:22:23.679
Antique nails...

00:22:27.807 --> 00:22:29.324
Almost as old as the car...

00:22:32.178 --> 00:22:33.276
30 years of--

00:22:33.276 --> 00:22:36.283
( negligence ) 

00:22:36.742 --> 00:22:38.323
I had to take everything out!

00:22:39.262 --> 00:22:44.285
Just to find this little piece of...

00:22:45.762 --> 00:22:46.832
I don't know what it is...

00:22:46.832 --> 00:22:48.904
Rope, or plastic?

00:22:48.904 --> 00:22:52.379
And, now we can reach what we were looking for...

00:22:53.185 --> 00:22:55.928
The wrench here, and the jack.

00:23:04.627 --> 00:23:06.787
Do you think your father will be watching the video?

00:23:08.935 --> 00:23:12.056
- if he is going to watch it?

00:23:12.056 --> 00:23:13.800
- I think so, yeah!

00:23:14.019 --> 00:23:16.400
He would have a lot of opinions!

00:23:16.868 --> 00:23:17.840
Yeah!

00:23:41.534 --> 00:23:42.684
Very heavy!

00:23:44.560 --> 00:23:46.560
Does it open?

00:23:46.560 --> 00:23:48.560
Yes of course

00:23:51.828 --> 00:23:53.414
That's no problem.

00:23:53.850 --> 00:23:55.327
If you're strong...

00:23:59.413 --> 00:24:00.367
Funny, funny, funny!

00:24:01.138 --> 00:24:06.683
We have the spare tire here, and we need 
to attach it to the bottom of the car.

00:24:07.169 --> 00:24:08.930
just put this in...

00:24:10.608 --> 00:24:12.103
start wrenching!

00:24:12.741 --> 00:24:14.313
I hope I didn't do anything

00:24:18.034 --> 00:24:19.745
I already oiled it.

00:24:22.150 --> 00:24:24.150
You see how smooth it is.

00:24:28.309 --> 00:24:30.050
And, this will stay in...

00:24:35.855 --> 00:24:40.651
The pipe is leaking every time you put diesel oil in it...

00:24:40.651 --> 00:24:46.381
The idea of this thing is to make a new connection,
 between these two.

00:24:46.840 --> 00:24:56.470
And, we've cut this in half, took this off,
make these two together, and mount it under the car.

00:25:13.040 --> 00:25:19.400
So, now it's like the old one, 
but only made of two pieces of...

00:25:21.505 --> 00:25:22.954
What's it called in English?

00:25:23.222 --> 00:25:23.890
- Pipe?

00:25:23.890 --> 00:25:24.693
Pipe!

00:25:25.096 --> 00:25:27.011
Two thin pieces of pipe...

00:25:43.514 --> 00:25:45.467
I'm satisfied with all the things we've done!

00:25:45.467 --> 00:25:49.105
Because, now, everything is repaired what was broken...

00:25:49.105 --> 00:25:49.605
- Yeah!

00:25:49.605 --> 00:25:50.563
And, that's good!

00:25:50.563 --> 00:25:51.063
- Yeah...

00:25:53.040 --> 00:25:59.141
We had some little issues with this dashboard,
that was a bit like broken, and all the plastic was old...

00:25:59.141 --> 00:26:02.806
So, now, we're gonna try to make something nice out of it!

00:26:02.806 --> 00:26:04.712
And, get a nice finishing..

00:26:04.712 --> 00:26:07.903
Something that is nice to drive behind...

00:26:07.903 --> 00:26:13.751
You can see the good views, 
plus the good looking, of the inside of the car, after this...

00:27:24.201 --> 00:27:27.440
Up and down, 
left and right!

00:28:07.654 --> 00:28:09.654
Woah!

00:28:11.093 --> 00:28:12.958
Yeaaah....

00:28:13.850 --> 00:28:14.722
Kevin!

00:28:14.722 --> 00:28:15.423
- Yeah?

00:28:15.423 --> 00:28:16.347
They found this!

00:28:17.271 --> 00:28:18.250
What do you think?

00:28:19.840 --> 00:28:20.726
Could you use them?

00:28:20.726 --> 00:28:21.920
- Yeah, yeah, yeah!

00:28:23.080 --> 00:28:24.070
They are so broken...

00:28:24.070 --> 00:28:25.388
They have some holes...

00:28:25.388 --> 00:28:27.418
- Yeah, their back is useful...

00:28:27.418 --> 00:28:29.014
The back is useful, eh?

00:28:29.282 --> 00:28:30.361
The front?

00:28:30.361 --> 00:28:32.004
- I don't want to look at you from the front...

00:28:32.004 --> 00:28:33.268
No?

00:28:36.147 --> 00:28:37.074
- Way too exposed!

00:28:37.074 --> 00:28:38.675
Okay, but you can use it?

00:28:38.675 --> 00:28:39.247
- Yeah!

00:28:39.247 --> 00:28:40.400
Nice!

00:30:25.179 --> 00:30:26.944
Ok!

00:30:27.659 --> 00:30:31.649
Okay, now that the work is done, 
let's have a drive-around to see how it feels.

00:30:52.899 --> 00:30:56.712
After the first test of the car, 
everything is starting good!

00:30:56.712 --> 00:30:58.143
Everything works!

00:30:58.143 --> 00:31:00.300
It seems that we put everything in place!

00:31:00.300 --> 00:31:01.976
It sounds better!

00:31:01.976 --> 00:31:03.656
It drives better!

00:31:03.656 --> 00:31:08.320
But now, we want to test it for real, on a dirt road.

00:31:42.364 --> 00:31:43.720
Thank you guys!

00:31:43.720 --> 00:31:46.068
We came to the local garage.

00:31:46.068 --> 00:31:51.013
And, we will replace our old tires, 
for something more suitable for our land...

00:32:21.510 --> 00:32:25.864
With the old tires, we will bring it back to the Kamp, 
to see what we can do with them.

00:32:26.669 --> 00:32:28.018
We will give it another try now.

00:32:28.018 --> 00:32:29.360
Let's see how it goes!

00:33:06.360 --> 00:33:07.510
It works!

00:33:07.778 --> 00:33:09.087
It works!

00:33:25.533 --> 00:33:28.749
So, it's been a hard work to renovate this car, but also fun!

00:33:29.554 --> 00:33:31.392
We love how it drives, and how it looks!

00:33:32.130 --> 00:33:34.968
We will check how it behaves during the season...

00:33:34.968 --> 00:33:37.722
But, at the moment, we are excited to have it ready!

00:33:48.640 --> 00:33:51.887
It's always difficult to choose between older, 
and less efficient stuff...

00:33:51.887 --> 00:33:53.861
Or, newer and more efficient.

00:33:56.600 --> 00:34:02.570
This time, we decide to give a new life to this old guy, 
since it's a better fit to our current situation.

00:34:03.226 --> 00:34:05.438
Curious to hear how you make these choices.

00:34:05.941 --> 00:34:08.079
For now, we will make the most out of it...

00:34:08.784 --> 00:34:11.200
And, hope it lasts many more years! 

00:34:22.777 --> 00:34:24.720
It works perfect!

00:35:00.640 --> 00:35:01.547
It's quite good!

00:35:02.185 --> 00:35:04.152
Everything works nice...

00:35:05.025 --> 00:35:07.740
No problems, and smooth...

00:35:08.640 --> 00:35:11.177
What else can you ask for?

